    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616-a8">

                <pb facs="0725" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg629"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The commission to Malietoa.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Apia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1899-05-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 30,
                    1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of May 29, we beg
                    to state that it is our intention to first take the arms and ammunition of the
                    Mataafa party, and after we have assured ourselves that they have disarmed, to
                    receive your arms and ammunition. Secondly, we shall take measures to preserve
                    order and protect every person in Mulinuu.</p>
                <p>We are, sir, yours, faithfully,</p>
                <closer>[Signed by the commissioners.]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
